# Claude Code local session state — not part of the marketplace
.claude/*
# ...except this repo's own mirrors of the skills it ships, which are versioned with
# the repo so they cannot silently drift from the plugin skills they mirror.
#
# The whole mirror directory is un-ignored, not one skill at a time. Allowlisting
# each skill by name meant a newly mirrored skill was silently untracked: `git add -A`
# skipped it without error and every local check passed, because the file was on disk.
# It took a CI run on a fresh checkout to notice. That is the failure mode this repo
# refuses to fix with a reminder.
#
# What this un-ignoring would otherwise risk — sweeping a contributor's project-local
# scratch skill into a commit — is covered by a mechanism rather than by scoping:
# scripts/verify-mirror.sh fails on any directory here with no counterpart under
# plugins/quick-dev/skills/, and now also on any mirrored file git is not tracking.
!.claude/skills/

node_modules/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
